<p>Pope Leo XIV used the final stop of his four-country Africa tour to press for freedom, justice, and a narrower gap between rich and poor during events in Equatorial Guinea on April 22. In Malabo, he said the country should serve the common good rather than private interests. He also criticized the &quot;colonisation&quot; of Africa’s minerals and what he called a &quot;lust for power,&quot; delivering that message in a nation led by President Teodoro Obiang Nguema Mbasogo since 1979. The visit drew large, enthusiastic crowds and marked the first papal trip to Equatorial Guinea since John Paul II visited in 1982, underscoring the stop’s symbolic weight for local Catholics. Leo’s remarks put inequality and governance at the center of his closing message in Africa, while also offering a hopeful call for believers to help bridge long-standing social divides.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/AuxdJSZ0LiiX976nkbQ7JZE7moNSdWte4X_MbeyfcJX2jtBAv2WuwxxBZETuyoTdPdOHttWre4Kvr6hIMIMePHry5PjwBDppUfyYN0VTxAq9dF2GIJw5a8Y6Wh1nAbPqXmfE0q5FQhbgrkbA3gE4x4scJAkj6jEHDKmo6_SMQnfAePVOnv57t9J-WM4Cf_TqhlV65k_GeQtRfu-h1Lz_5V5-RYzP1oJ92W3AbVKHa2FBfw3Iga3iwl3zx7C92ZpZ7PeRrU8iGXgHlkNdkg' alt='Pope Leo XIV arrives at the Basilica of the Immaculate Conception, in Mongomo, Equatorial Guinea, on Wednesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Mass audience: Leo celebrated Mass with members of the presidential family present, giving his appeal for justice and fairness added political visibility in the country.</li><li>Catholic majority: Euronews said roughly three-fourths of Equatorial Guinea’s population is Catholic, helping explain the scale of the public welcome for the pope.</li><li>Tour finale: The stop in Equatorial Guinea concluded a four-country African trip, making the speech his last major message of the tour.</li><li>Public reception: Crowds lined the road from the airport into Malabo, cheering and waving flags as Leo arrived in the administrative capital.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pope Leo XIV: He urged Equatorial Guineans to work for freedom and justice and to narrow the gap between the privileged and the disadvantaged, framing social inequality as a moral challenge for believers. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/pope-visiting-equatorial-guinea-prison-spotlight-after-us-132263818'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Catholic faithful in Equatorial Guinea: Supporters turned out in large numbers along the route into Malabo, giving the pope an enthusiastic welcome on a visit many had never seen in their lifetime. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3350961/pope-leo-denounces-colonisation-minerals-final-leg-africa-tour'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>News coverage of the visit: Several outlets framed the pope’s final-day message as a direct denunciation of inequality and entrenched power, with governance and resource exploitation emerging as the defining themes of the stop. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/22/pope-leo-xiv-condemns-lust-for-power-and-inequality-in-equatorial-guinea'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3350961/pope-leo-denounces-colonisation-minerals-final-leg-africa-tour'>Pope Leo denounces ‘colonisation’ of minerals on final leg of Africa tour</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/pope-decries-inequality-on-whirlwind-last-day-of-africa-tour'>Pope Leo decries inequality on whirlwind last day of Africa tour</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/pope-visiting-equatorial-guinea-prison-spotlight-after-us-132263818'>Pope calls for justice and closing income gap in Equatorial Guinea Mass with presidential family</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/22/pope-leo-xiv-condemns-lust-for-power-and-inequality-in-equatorial-guinea'>Pope Leo XIV condemns ‘lust for power’ and inequality in Equatorial Guinea</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-pope-leo-equatorial-guinea-africa-tour/'>Pope Leo calls for justice and closing income gap on final leg of Africa tour</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/africa-pope-equatorial-guinea-0134a6982c295c125259c5fa4eb73395'>Pope Leo XIV arrives in Malabo, the final leg of his papal visit to Africa, becoming the first pope to visit Equatorial Guinea since John Paul II in 1982.</a> - apnews.com</li></ul>